# Shell scripts must reach the guest with LF endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is on for this checkout, and a corpus case checked out with
# CRLF fails INSIDE tobyOS in a way that looks like a shell bug: the guest's
# bash sees the stray CR and exits 2 with a syntax error, while MSYS bash on
# the host tolerates it and reports the same file as fine. That cost a full
# build-and-boot cycle to track down once already.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The busybox applet list is read line-by-line by the initrd rule to create
# one hard link per name. A CRLF checkout cost a build cycle here too, and in
# a nastier way than the scripts above: MSYS resolves "bin/ls\r" as if the CR
# were not there, so `[ -e ]` answered TRUE for all 400 names, every one was
# skipped as "already taken", and the build reported success having linked
# nothing. The rule strips a trailing CR defensively as well.
programs/busybox/applets.txt text eol=lf
